== R5: midpoint family P_s = z^N - lam z^{N-1} + lam z - 1
  N= 3: max rel. diff |disc| closed form vs Sylvester determinant = 4.1e-49
  N= 4: max rel. diff |disc| closed form vs Sylvester determinant = 2.5e-49
  N= 5: max rel. diff |disc| closed form vs Sylvester determinant = 7.1e-49
  N= 7: max rel. diff |disc| closed form vs Sylvester determinant = 8.9e-50
  N= 9: max rel. diff |disc| closed form vs Sylvester determinant = 2.6e-48
  N=12: max rel. diff |disc| closed form vs Sylvester determinant = 9.7e-49
  first-collision claim: g_lam(x) = 2 cos((N-1)x/2) + (1-lam) sin((N-2)x/2)/sin(x/2) at x_k = 2 pi k/(N-1)
     max |g_lam(x_k) - (-1)^k (1+lam)|/(1+lam) over N in {3..4000} = 1.1e-13;  g_lam(0) = 2-(lam-1)(N-2) > 0 iff lam < N/(N-2)
     => for every lam < N/(N-2) the real function g_lam alternates in sign at the N points x_0..x_{N-1} of [0,2pi],
        so G has N-1 distinct roots on the circle, none equal to 1: no collision before the triple one. [P]
